CORE no-wide-pointer-encoding
main.c
--no-standard-checks
^Replaced MMIO operations: 3 read\(s\), 1 write\(s\)
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Partially broken under --wide-pointer-encoding. Reads of device addresses
are now routed to the handler (is_integer_address recognises the integer
address; see regression test mm_io2). The write `p[0]=2` to the device
address, however, can corrupt a real object the solver places at that flat
address, because the wide encoding deliberately lets integer addresses
alias real objects (issue #8200) and has no notion yet of valid
integer-address regions. Full support awaits issue #6747's --mmio-region.
